    <!-- #540 — Package.Tests is a MEMBER, and that is the whole point. It used to be excluded to keep
         release-scoped checks off the PR, but the effect was that its ~325 working-tree rules ran in
         ZERO gate cadences: every one of them fired after the merge that broke it, never on the PR.
         The release-scoped checks in here are already deferred behind env flags the release lane sets
         (FS_SKIA_RUN_PACKAGE_CONSUMER_SMOKE, FS_GG_RUN_TEMPLATE_PAYLOAD_RESTORE), so membership costs
         the gate ~4s and buys it every rule that a PR can actually break. See tests/Package.Tests/Tests.fs.

         #613 — and this line is now LOAD-BEARING for more than itself. Fifteen `*CoherenceTests.fs`
         twins existed only to hoist rules out of this project back when it was excluded; #613 deleted
         them because membership already puts those rules on the PR gate. Remove this entry and they do
         not merely stop running here — they stop running on the PR at all, with no twin left to catch
         it. `PackageTestsGateMembershipTests` asserts this membership so that removal reds instead of
         passing quietly; if you are excluding Package.Tests deliberately, restore the twins in the same
         PR. -->
    <Project Path="tests/Package.Tests/Package.Tests.fsproj" />
